    "status": "present",
    "value": "Design a writer class that holds an in-memory buffer of a fixed byte capacity in front of an output sink. write(data) appends the bytes in order; whenever the buffer becomes completely full it is immediately emptied into the sink, so a single long write can empty the buffer several times. flush() empties whatever is currently buffered, even if the buffer is not full. Because the real sink is not observable in a test, each method returns a new list of exactly the bytes passed to the sink during that call, or an empty list when nothing was passed. The class may also be given a sink object whose write(byte) method receives each byte as it is emptied."
  },
